<newsitem itemid="190299" id="root" date="1996-11-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Northumbrian Water H1 profits 74 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Northumbrian Water H1 profits 74 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year to 30 September</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.4</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	  4.85*</p>
<p> Pretax		     74.3</p>
<p> Turnover		  274.0</p>
<p> Operating profit	 98.7</p>
<p> Interest		   24.5</p>
<p> Exceptional charge	3.8</p>
<p> Tax			  10.8</p>
<p>NOTE -- First published results of new Northumbrian Water Group. Northumbrian Water Ltd is merging with the water business of former North East Water. Northumbrian Water is part of Lyonnaise des Eaux. * NOTE - The company is also declaring a second interim dividend of 0.24 pence per share. Both interim dividends will be payable on December 16 to shareholders on the register on November 25. The company said it still plans to declare a total dividend of 9.70p per share for the year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
